Perfect! The firmware has extracted cleanly, and we have boot.img right where we need it (alongside vbmeta.img, which we will also need to keep things stable).
Let's push boot.img to your phone and clear the verification security.
------------------------------
## Step 1: Send boot.img to your Phone
Make sure your phone is booted up normally, connected to your computer via USB, and that USB Debugging is turned on in your phone's Developer Options.
Run this command to copy the file directly to your phone's Download folder:

adb push Tecno_Firmware/boot.img /sdcard/Download/

------------------------------
## Step 2: Patch it with Magisk on your Phone

   1. Disconnect your phone (or leave it plugged in) and open the Magisk App on your device.
   2. Tap Install (the top one, next to Magisk).
   3. Select Select and Patch a File.
   4. Use your phone's file manager to go to your Downloads folder and select boot.img.
   5. Tap LET'S GO.
   6. Once it says "All done!", look at the log on your phone screen. It will tell you the name of the new file it created, usually something like:
   magisk_patched_XXXXX.img

------------------------------
## Step 3: Pull the Patched File Back to Ubuntu
Connect your phone back to the computer and pull that modified file into your terminal directory:

adb pull /sdcard/Download/magisk_patched_*.img .

(Note the dot . at the end of the command—it tells Ubuntu to copy the file to your current ~/Downloads folder).
